<div class="prose-block">

<p>I open the laptop again, this time for shopping instead of research. Might as well handle the rest of the list while I'm at it.</p>

<p>A hairbrush, a basic paddle brush, $8.99. I need this desperately. My hair has been tangled since Day 1, and my fingers are not adequate tools for detangling.</p>

<p>A women's razor, the kind with the moisture strip and the pivoting head, $6.99 for a starter pack. I haven't shaved my legs yet, but the hair is lighter and finer than Marcus's ever was. Still visible, though. I'll deal with it eventually.</p>

<p>I click into a solo video by accident while comparing brush reviews, a woman on a bed using a small vibrator, circling her clit the same way I do with two fingers, except the vibrator adds a frequency of stimulation I can't replicate by hand. Something in my brain files it away as a thing I want.</p>

<p>I open a shopping app and search "bullet vibrator." The first result is $15.99, matte purple, rechargeable, whisper quiet, ten vibration patterns. The reviews are five stars across the board, from women with names like SatisfiedSarah87 saying things like "changed my life."</p>

<p>I scroll through women's underwear afterward, more curiosity than need, lace, thongs, boy shorts, cheeky cuts, in more colors than I knew underwear even came in. Marcus owned boxers. That was the whole list. I bookmark a set of black lace panties for twelve dollars and don't buy them yet. Not tonight.</p>

</div>

