:: D03_PornExplore [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The laptop is open on the bed. The apartment is dark except for the screen glow. I've locked the front door and checked it twice. The curtains are drawn.</p>

<p>I open an incognito tab and go to a site I've been to a thousand times as Marcus. The interface is the same. The categories are the same. The thumbnails of bodies doing things to other bodies are the same. But I'm different, and that changes everything.</p>

<p>I click on what Marcus used to watch, straight, male POV, the camera behind the man's shoulder so you see the woman from his angle. My response is immediate and confusing. I'm aroused, but the arousal has shifted. I'm not watching the woman the way Marcus watched women, as an object of desire external to himself. I'm watching her the way you watch someone demonstrate a skill you're trying to learn, the angle of her legs, the sounds she makes. When she moans, I feel a sympathetic vibration in my own throat.</p>

<p>The man on screen is a different kind of problem. I look at his arms and something tightens below my navel. Is this attraction? I don't know. It might be fascination, or envy, or something else that doesn't have a word yet.</p>

<p>I click away and open a different category. Two women.</p>

<p>The effect is instant. Heat blooms between my legs before the video is ten seconds in. Two women kissing, slow and deliberate, hands exploring curves that mirror my own. This feels different, more resonant, more personal. I'm watching two bodies that look like mine doing things I can imagine being done to me, and the line between watching and imagining starts dissolving. When one woman's mouth finds the other's nipple, I feel my own nipples stiffen under my t-shirt.</p>

<p>I watch for ten minutes. I don't touch myself, because this isn't supposed to be about getting off. This is supposed to be about understanding what turns me on and why. Research, clinical and methodical.</p>

<p>My panties are soaked by minute seven. So much for clinical.</p>

<p>I click into solo female content next, a woman alone on a bed touching herself with a small vibrator held just beside her clit instead of directly on it. She comes and squirts, clear fluid soaking the sheet under her hips, and something in my chest loosens watching it. So it is a thing. I am not broken. I am not some medical anomaly leaking on my own mattress. Women just do this.</p>

<p>I click again, half on purpose now, and land on a compilation of women giving head. My whole perspective has shifted without me noticing it happen. I'm not imagining receiving anymore, I'm imagining giving, the weight of someone on my tongue, my lips stretching around him, what my own mouth would even feel like doing that. I touch my lips with two fingers. Fuller than they used to be. I don't finish that thought. I don't stop the video either.</p>

<p>My body responds to women, strongly, viscerally, with the kind of immediate arousal that doesn't leave room for ambiguity. My body also responds to men, but differently. More tentatively. A question mark instead of an exclamation point.</p>

<p>I don't know what that makes me. The old labels feel like clothes that don't fit. Marcus was straight the way a wall is straight, and he never questioned it because there was nothing to question. But Mia's body has its own opinions and its own desires, and they don't align neatly with anything Marcus knew.</p>

<p>I'll figure it out. Not tonight. But I'll figure it out.</p>

</div>

